### 2. Build the scaffoldReadme helpers — deriveProjectName and insertBadge

Read: `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`, `coding-playbook/architecture/folder-structure`

- [x] 2a. Create `src/tools/init/scaffoldReadme/deriveProjectName/index.ts`. Default export `deriveProjectName(projectRoot: string): Promise<string>`. Reads `package.json` from `projectRoot` — if it exists and has a `name` field, return that name. Otherwise, derive from the folder name: take `basename(projectRoot)`, split on hyphens, title-case each word, join with spaces. JSDoc explains the two-source fallback and why package.json is preferred (authored name vs folder convention).
- [x] 2b. Create `src/tools/init/scaffoldReadme/insertBadge/index.ts`. Default export `insertBadge(content: string): string`. This is the existing `insertBadge` function lifted verbatim from `src/tools/init/injectBadge/index.ts` (the two-phase frontmatter-skip then badge-strip-count scan). Also export the two constants `BADGE_LINE` and `BADGE_DETECTION` as named exports from this file — they are consumed by the orchestrator for detection and by the README creation path.

### 3. Build the scaffoldReadme orchestrator

Read: `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`, `coding-playbook/architecture/folder-structure`

- [x] Create `src/tools/init/scaffoldReadme/index.ts`. Default export `scaffoldReadme(projectRoot: string): Promise<InitStep>`. Import `deriveProjectName` from `./deriveProjectName/index.js`, `insertBadge`, `BADGE_LINE`, and `BADGE_DETECTION` from `./insertBadge/index.js`.
- [x] The function follows a single conditional gate: check if `README.md` exists at `projectRoot`.
- [x] **README absent (create path):** Call `deriveProjectName(projectRoot)` to get the project name. Compose the full README content: `BADGE_LINE`, blank line, `# {projectName}`, blank line, `A brief description of what this project does.`, trailing newline. Return `InitStep` with `name: "README"`, `status: "would-create"`, `category: "readme"`, `filePath` pointing to `README.md`, and `content` set to the composed text.
- [x] **README present:** Read its content. If it includes `BADGE_DETECTION`, return `InitStep` with `name: "README badge"`, `status: "exists"`, `category: "readme"`, `filePath` set, no content. If the badge is absent, call `insertBadge(content)` and return `InitStep` with `name: "README badge"`, `status: "would-create"`, `category: "readme"`, `filePath` set, `content` set to the modified text.
- [x] The function never returns `would-skip` — unlike `injectBadge`, this category always has work to do or the work is already done. The two statuses are `would-create` and `exists`.

